> WALDW[ICK], N.J. -- Thomas J. McL[aughlin], of Waldwick, died Thursday, Nov. 17. He was 86.
Born in the Bronx, in 1930, he was a longtime resident of Waldwick. He was a construction supervisor at AJ Contracting in Manhattan, before retiring. He served in the U.S. Army during peacetime.
He is survived by his wife, Theresa F. McL[aughlin]; children, Thomas J. McL[aughlin] Jr. and his wife Jayne, Theresa Karole, Michael McL[aughlin], Ma[ureen] McGinle and her husband Lawrence and Ellen M. McL[aughlin]; grandchildren, Katherine, Devin, Thomas, John, Michael and Ashley; and sister, Mary Kate Jensen.
Visitation will from 2-5 p.m. Sunday at the Vander Plaat Funeral Home, 257 God[win] Ave., Wy[ck]off. A funeral Mass will be celebrated at 11 a.m. Monday at Church of the Nativity, 315 Prospect St., Midland Park. Interment will follow at Ascension Cemetery in M[onse]y, N.Y.

